{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "scenario_id": "dates_before_gregorian_cutover",
  "title": "Rows with dates before the Gregorian calendar cutover are appended",
  "category": "temporal",
  "description": "v0 has three rows with recent dates. v1 keeps them and appends four rows dated 0001-01-01, 1000-01-01, 1500-06-15 and 1582-10-04, each as a date32 and as a naive timestamp at noon of that day. The schema is unchanged.",
  "notes": [
    "All values are proleptic Gregorian, as Parquet DATE and TIMESTAMP define them: days and microseconds since 1970-01-01. 1582-10-04 is the day before the 1582-10-15 Gregorian cutover.",
    "A reader that converts dates before the cutover to the Julian calendar (a hybrid calendar) reads the four appended rows as different days; the three v0 rows are unaffected."
  ],
